Package: miadi-tmux
Version: 3.7c-4
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34), libevent-core-2.1-7 (>= 2.1.8-stable), libtinfo6 (>= 6)
Provides: tmux (= 3.7c)
Conflicts: tmux
Replaces: tmux
Maintainer: Miadi <mia@jgwill.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/jgwill/miadi-orchestration-kit
Description: tmux 3.7c for a Miadi host, in place of the distribution's tmux
 Ubuntu 22.04 ships tmux 3.2a. A tmux client cannot attach to a server of
 another version ("open terminal failed: not a terminal"), so a Miadi host
 runs one tmux. This package is the upstream release built for the host:
 /usr/bin/tmux and its manual. It replaces the distribution's tmux package,
 and packages that depend on tmux (tmuxinator, miadi-tide) take this one.
 .
 One patch: a session name may contain colons, such as a circle id
 (circle:1791110394383:jj1ql8), and still be a target: tmux attach -t
 a:b:c finds session a:b:c instead of window b:c of session a.
